<%# Shown when this step has no content yet AND this user is not authorized to
    commission new generation for it — today that means the route's purchase was
    refunded (reads survive a refund by approved policy; new AI spend does not).

    Deliberately NOT `_content_failed`: that partial says "we couldn't build this
    lesson" and offers a retry button. Both would be untrue here. Nothing failed,
    and no amount of retrying will produce the lesson, because the decision is a
    policy one and not a transient error. A spinner would be worse still — the
    poll endpoint re-runs load_step_content, so an unauthorized step would spin
    every 3s forever against a decision that will never change on its own.

    The step's existing content, where there is any, is untouched and still
    rendered by the normal branches of _step_content_frame. %>

<div style="max-width:560px; margin:48px auto; padding:28px 32px; border-radius:14px;
            background:var(--color-surface-muted, rgba(120,120,120,0.05));
            border:1px solid var(--color-border-subtle, rgba(120,120,120,0.16));
            font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif; text-align:center;">

  <div style="font-size:1.6rem; margin-bottom:10px;">🔒</div>

  <h2 style="font-size:1.05rem; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 10px;
             color:var(--color-text-primary, #2C2C2C);">
    <%= t("learning_engine.content_unavailable.title") %>
  </h2>

  <p style="font-size:0.85rem; line-height:1.55; margin:0 0 20px;
            color:var(--color-text-secondary, #6B6B6B);">
    <%= t("learning_engine.content_unavailable.body") %>
  </p>

  <div style="margin-top:18px;">
    <%= link_to t("learning_engine.content_unavailable.back"),
                route_path(@route),
                style: "font-size:0.78rem; color:var(--color-text-secondary, #6B6B6B);" %>
  </div>
</div>
